{"id": "EUVD-2026-87069", "enisaUuid": "e946247b-4365-37d2-ba24-1c95fc251493", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: platform: Use acpi_bus_get_primary_device()\n\nThe acpi_get_first_physical_node() usage in acpi_platform_fill_resource()\nand acpi_create_platform_device() is generally unsafe because in theory\nthe device returned by it may be freed at any time [1].\n\nIt is also inefficient because acpi_get_first_physical_node() is called\nmultiple times for the same argument which can be avoided.\n\nAddress these issues by using acpi_bus_get_primary_device() instead of\nacpi_get_first_physical_node() and adjusting the code to call it just\nonce at the beginning of and acpi_create_platform_device() and drop\nthe device reference acquired by it upon the return from that function.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T13:06:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:38:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a75e5de593ef158feb17989bff7730c5a3d82503", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/527a497fb2ef77a95170eefe2007e2c4c957bd2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9d202d3b6c28e8c779cd2f2b10d2f7ab665ca71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9ba4dd2f18bf3f439d9ef0d8f375f90360ba1bd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-100072", "GHSA-g9pc-522f-qjj8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2dd11c24-465f-3e9a-8460-f56e8079cf48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3d375d4a-aa96-385d-8d25-4f5bb36e0d29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b95bd160547f56a68aeb972c33ae9511e7a8380 <a75e5de593ef158feb17989bff7730c5a3d82503"}, {"id": "42c1d613-e0da-30e3-bcc1-746f49f84c22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "60ec7fa7-361f-352e-993f-d60d1f93a6b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 